// The cross-section lies in the y-z plane and is extruded along +x. Coordinates are in metres.
//
// ---- Layout: 5 vertical strips x 6 rows ------------------------------------------
// Six lines run from the top (z = 0) to the bottom (z = -0.025). Strip s lies between
// line s and line s+1 (counting from the left, y < 0). Rows are the cross-lines that join
// the vertices of the six lines; row r is the same cross-line in every strip.
//
//   line  z = 0        z = -0.025     passes through
//   1     -0.02        -0.03          flared left wall
//   2     -0.000449    -0.007781      left wall of the 0.3 mm channel
//   3     -0.000097    -0.00743       right wall of the 0.3 mm channel
//   4      0.005       -0.00643       reservoir left wall (above it a straight cut to P4)
//   5      0.008623     0.0125        reservoir right wall
//   6      0.02         0.03          flared right wall
//
//   row (from the bottom)   z range
//   0  bottom band           -0.025   to -0.02
//   1  thin layer            -0.02    to -0.0197
//   2  lower                 -0.0197  to the P14-P7 / W-P2 level
//   3  middle                that level to the N4 / P4 level
//   4  upper                 N4 / P4 level to the strip underside (z = -0.00045)
//   5  strip layer           -0.00045 to 0
//
// Because adjacent strips share the vertices on their common line, every block in a strip
// has the same y count and every block in a row has the same z count.
